  "reference": {
    "source": "lengthM (263 m overall) and beamM (38.9 m) from the English Wikipedia article 'Yamato-class battleship', read 2026-09-26. U.S. Naval Technical Mission to Japan reports Yamato and Musashi at 63,000 tons standard, 73,000 tons full load, and 28 kn; maxSpeedMps uses that primary postwar report (converted with 1 kn = 0.514444 m/s), read 2026-09-26. deckHeightM and turnRateRadPerS (0.75 deg/s) are ESTIMATES. hullHp (ten 1,000 lb bombs) is a gameplay choice. ARMAMENT (Track M, M1, read 2026-10-08): the model is Musashi (Ruling R4 keeps it), carried at her Leyte Gulf fit: three triple 46 cm turrets; the two centerline triple 15.5 cm turrets that the April 1944 refit kept (the wing turrets removed); six twin 12.7 cm mounts, as the model draws them (the refit's twelve twins are not modeled); and about 130 x 25 mm in triple and single mounts (English Wikipedia 'Japanese battleship Musashi', whose Armament section gives 115 and Service section 130). Every turret and mount is carved from the model at its own position: the 18 shielded 25 mm triples as one kit, the remaining ~76 singles as four static galleries of 19 (ESTIMATED positions on the model's decks)."
